 "report": {
  "summary": "Alcaraz leads the career head-to-head 10 wins to 7 over 17 matches. On clay the two are close, with Alcaraz ahead 3 wins to 2 over 5 matches. Sinner won the latest meeting, the Monte Carlo final in April 2026. Over the last two years both have very strong clay records, and Alcaraz's 2024-26 clay win rate is slightly higher than Sinner's. Sinner serves better on clay.",
  "strengths": [
   "Alcaraz has won 27 of 29 clay matches (93.1%) from 2024-10-26 to 2026-10-26. That is a small sample.",
   "He puts 65.7% of first serves in on clay (29 matches), against 61.4% for Sinner.",
   "He has won 3 of the 5 clay meetings with Sinner, including the 2025 Roland Garros final and the 2025 Rome final.",
   "He is in form: 9 wins in his last 10 matches, including the Vienna title on hard courts. This is a small sample.",
   "He saves break points on clay at 65.7% (169 break points faced, 29 matches), against 64.5% for Sinner."
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
   "His clay serve is weaker than Sinner's. He wins 64.5% of service points, against 69.8% for Sinner. He wins 56.5% of second-serve points, against 60.4% for Sinner.",
   "He hits 2.5 aces per match on clay, against 4.5 for Sinner.",
   "He lost the 2026 Monte Carlo final to Sinner in straight sets (7-6(5) 6-3).",
   "Sinner leads the grass head-to-head 2-0, but that is only 2 matches and not relevant on clay.",
   "His clay return points won (45.1%) are about level with Sinner's (44.4%), so he gets no clear return edge."
  ],
  "game_plan": [
   "Hold serve through first-serve points. Sinner wins 75.7% of first-serve points on clay (32 matches), against 68.7% for Alcaraz. Coaching inference: protect that first-serve edge to keep the pressure on Alcaraz's serve.",
   "Attack Alcaraz's second serve. He wins 56.5% of second-serve points on clay, against 60.4% for Sinner. Coaching inference: step in and return aggressively on second serves.",
   "Convert break points. Both players convert about 46% on clay (Sinner 46.0%, Alcaraz 46.2%), so chances will be scarce. Coaching inference: be ready for the few break points that come.",
   "Use the Monte Carlo 2026 template, which Sinner won 7-6(5) 6-3. Expect tight sets: three of the five clay meetings went to a deciding tiebreak or went the distance. Coaching inference: prepare for tiebreaks and long matches.",
   "Do not read much into the Roland Garros loss to Cerundolo. It was Sinner's only recent clay loss in the last-10 list, and it is a small sample."
  ],
